 "intro": {
  "text": "The Caro-Kann prepares ...d5 with the c-pawn ready to take back, so Black keeps a share of the centre and makes f7 safer. Unlike the French (1...e6), it does not shut in the light-squared bishop, though the knight loses the c6 square. It has a reputation as a solid, defensive reply to 1.e4.",
