     "notes": {
      "text": "4...Bf5, the Classical Variation, develops your bishop and attacks the e4 knight; the bishop will later control the long diagonal from g6 and then h7. 4...Nf6 5.Nxf6+ leaves you with doubled pawns, and 4...Nd7 (Karpov Variation) looks slower because the knight must move again before that bishop can come out.",
